data_ARG
#
_chem_comp.id                  ARG
_chem_comp.name                'ARG side chain, Protonated'
_chem_comp.type                non-polymer
_chem_comp.formula             'C4 H12 N3'
_chem_comp.pdbx_formal_charge  1
#
# Cbeta-capped side-chain fragment, generated from the wwPDB Chemical
# Component Dictionary entry ARG by scripts/build_fragment_cifs.py.
# Backbone atoms are removed and CB carries a hydrogen in place of CA.
#
# _chem_comp_atom below is the molecule's only atom list. An atom is
# addressed by its position in it, counting from 0, and that same number
# is the atom's index in the graph config, in the assembly component and
# in the ORCA input. Nothing renumbers it on the way. The file therefore
# carries no _atom_site loop and no pdbx_ordinal, because either would be
# a second numbering that could disagree with this one.
#
# The chemistry above is the dictionary's. The coordinates below are NOT:
# they are this fragment optimised at XTB2 with ALPB(thf), the surface assemble docks on, at the charge and
# multiplicity it declares (+1, 1).
#
# The dictionary could not supply them. A protonation variant is made by
# deleting a hydrogen, which does not move the heavy atoms the dictionary
# placed around it, so the fragment would declare one charge while carrying
# the geometry of another: CCD GLU is the neutral acid, and dropping HE2
# leaves a C=O at 1.21 A and a C-OH at 1.34 A opened to 120 degrees where a
# carboxylate is symmetric at 1.26 A and 129 degrees. At QM level that is a
# different molecule, and it behaves like one -- ORCA's DOCKER rejected every
# pose of such a glutamate, because the restrained hydroxyl-type oxygen took
# the substrate's proton back and broke the topology.
#
# They are written to the _ideal columns because that is where biotite and
# the GUI parser read coordinates from, not as a claim that the dictionary
# idealised them. There is no second, experimental set: a Cbeta-capped side
# chain has never been in a crystal.
#
# Connectivity was read back off the optimised geometry and matched the
# bonds below, so this is the same molecule that went in.
#
loop_
_pdbx_chem_comp_descriptor.comp_id
_pdbx_chem_comp_descriptor.type
_pdbx_chem_comp_descriptor.program
_pdbx_chem_comp_descriptor.descriptor
ARG SMILES RDKit 'CCCNC(N)=[NH2+]'
#
loop_
_chem_comp_atom.comp_id
_chem_comp_atom.atom_id
_chem_comp_atom.type_symbol
_chem_comp_atom.charge
_chem_comp_atom.pdbx_aromatic_flag
_chem_comp_atom.pdbx_model_Cartn_x_ideal
_chem_comp_atom.pdbx_model_Cartn_y_ideal
_chem_comp_atom.pdbx_model_Cartn_z_ideal
